      <uighur>qayidaq</uighur>
      <cyrillic>хайдаг</cyrillic>
      <transcript>XAIDAΓ</transcript>
      <definition>adj. and n. Lone, single; isolated elevation; peak rising from a plain; milch animal whose young has been weaned or has died.</definition>
      <page>912</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠶᠢᠳᠠᠬ ᠮᠣᠳᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- modu</transcript>
          <definition> Lonely or isolated tree.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠶᠢᠳᠠᠬ ᠮᠣᠷᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- mori</transcript>
          <definition> A single horse.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠬᠠᠶᠢᠳᠠᠬ ᠦᠨᠢᠶ᠎ᠡ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- ynij-e</transcript>
          <definition> Milch cow whose calf has been weaned or has died.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
